WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.042 --> 00:00:02.211
What just happened?
What did you do?

00:00:02.294 --> 00:00:03.212
What's happening?

00:00:03.879 --> 00:00:05.214
That, that's what
I'd like to know.

00:00:05.297 --> 00:00:07.216
It's only
ever been about me.

00:00:07.299 --> 00:00:09.092
About trying to be me.

00:00:09.176 --> 00:00:10.802
We are each other.

00:00:10.886 --> 00:00:13.597
A threat to one of us
is a threat to us both.

00:00:14.765 --> 00:00:15.724
What are you doing?

00:00:16.308 --> 00:00:19.186
Would you believe
I'm having a bad day?

00:00:22.856 --> 00:00:25.150
It started when Bonnie
denied me my silence

00:00:25.234 --> 00:00:26.944
-like immortality.
-Of course.

00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:28.612
Because Katherine Pierce
can't be having

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:30.614
the good old
vampire-calibre mortality.

00:00:37.913 --> 00:00:39.665
I deserved it.

00:00:39.748 --> 00:00:41.625
I never had a graduation
or a prom

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:42.876
or, you know, a life.

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:44.294
But you did!

00:00:45.671 --> 00:00:47.422
You have everything.

00:00:47.506 --> 00:00:49.508
And it's not because
you're a good little girl

00:00:49.591 --> 00:00:52.678
who deserves happiness,
it's because you stole mine!

00:00:55.806 --> 00:00:57.432
I stole your happiness?

00:00:58.392 --> 00:00:59.476
You killed my brother.

00:01:03.105 --> 00:01:05.566
I'll admit, that was nasty.

00:01:17.035 --> 00:01:19.788
I have nothing

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:23.542
But I'm about
to change that.

00:01:27.629 --> 00:01:29.089
Kicking someone
while they're down,

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:31.425
classy till the end,
Katherine.

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:33.886
Your end.

00:01:40.642 --> 00:01:41.476
How are you?

00:01:42.227 --> 00:01:45.814
Good. Great.
You know, same as you.

00:01:45.898 --> 00:01:46.773
Living my best life.

00:01:46.857 --> 00:01:48.942
That is amazing, Sabrina.

00:01:49.026 --> 00:01:50.110
Yeah, I know it is.

00:01:51.486 --> 00:01:53.155
Except for this pool
of absolute darkness

00:01:53.238 --> 00:01:54.907
in the minds that's gonna
consume Greendale

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:56.700
and the entire world,
if we don't stop it.

00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:58.619
With a light that's bright
enough to banish it.

00:01:59.369 --> 00:02:01.955
Like? Morningstar bright?

00:02:02.039 --> 00:02:04.124
Yes.
And I can't do it alone.

00:02:04.875 --> 00:02:07.044
But if the two of us
can invoke the Unholy Power

00:02:07.127 --> 00:02:08.879
of our birthright,
it might work.

00:02:10.130 --> 00:02:11.131
Will you help me?

00:02:13.842 --> 00:02:14.885
We are each other.

00:02:15.469 --> 00:02:17.846
A threat to one of us,
is a threat to us both.

00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:23.060
I'm putting this down.

00:02:23.977 --> 00:02:25.145
Okay?

00:02:25.229 --> 00:02:26.146
It's okay.

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:27.564
It's okay.

00:02:31.068 --> 00:02:32.903
-What are you?
-I don't want any trouble.

00:02:33.529 --> 00:02:34.738
I don't know
what's happening,

00:02:35.614 --> 00:02:37.574
I would just like you
to leave my house, please.

00:02:37.658 --> 00:02:39.159
You leave this house.

00:02:40.285 --> 00:02:41.828
In fact, what are you
even doing here?

00:02:42.412 --> 00:02:43.288
I live here.

00:02:44.122 --> 00:02:45.165
I live here!

00:02:45.791 --> 00:02:47.751
-I live here!
-Take it easy. Take it easy.

00:02:47.835 --> 00:02:48.669
What's happening?

00:02:49.253 --> 00:02:50.546
What's happening...

00:02:50.629 --> 00:02:52.005
That's what
I'd like to know.

00:02:52.089 --> 00:02:53.173
That's what
I'd like to know.

00:02:53.841 --> 00:02:54.883
That's what
I'd like to know.

00:02:54.967 --> 00:02:56.343
The only thing I know

00:02:56.426 --> 00:02:58.011
is that I was upstairs
with my wife...

00:02:58.095 --> 00:03:00.764
Hold on. Your wife?

00:03:00.848 --> 00:03:01.807
And now I'm being attacked

00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:03.183
by someone
who looks like me.

00:03:04.852 --> 00:03:05.686
In a diaper.

00:03:06.311 --> 00:03:07.563
Well, all I know...

00:03:09.898 --> 00:03:12.192
is that I went to a spa,

00:03:12.901 --> 00:03:14.152
I woke up in a grave,

00:03:15.070 --> 00:03:18.198
and then I walked barefoot
for six hours...

00:03:18.907 --> 00:03:21.952
to find,
whatever the fuck you are,

00:03:22.035 --> 00:03:23.871
upstairs with my wife!

00:03:23.954 --> 00:03:25.372
I woke up in a spa.

00:03:26.415 --> 00:03:28.917
But then I went to work,
came home,

00:03:30.335 --> 00:03:31.336
and now this...

00:03:34.006 --> 00:03:35.215
-A spa.
-A spa...

00:03:36.341 --> 00:03:37.593
Bette...

00:03:38.719 --> 00:03:39.720
Dot...

00:03:40.846 --> 00:03:43.140
You have to come with me.
Now.

00:03:43.223 --> 00:03:45.100
You don't give the orders
in this house.

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:49.313
Dot, I know
you have mixed feelings.

00:03:49.396 --> 00:03:50.856
You're thinking
of getting the surgery,

00:03:50.939 --> 00:03:52.232
which I'll never allow.

00:03:52.316 --> 00:03:53.734
'Cause you'd never
cut a girl in half

00:03:53.817 --> 00:03:55.861
-would you, Dandy?
-Shut up!

00:03:55.944 --> 00:03:57.779
Stop trying
to ruin everything!

00:03:58.488 --> 00:04:00.240
How do you know, Dandy?

00:04:02.618 --> 00:04:03.869
About the surgery?

00:04:04.912 --> 00:04:07.539
I told you there will be
no secrets between us.

00:04:09.166 --> 00:04:10.542
You read my diary.

00:04:14.004 --> 00:04:15.214
I want to leave.

00:04:15.297 --> 00:04:16.340
She can't leave
without Bette.

00:04:16.423 --> 00:04:17.716
We're in love.

00:04:17.799 --> 00:04:20.260
And love trumps everything.

00:04:20.844 --> 00:04:22.721
Your mother said
the girls could go anytime.

00:04:22.804 --> 00:04:23.889
Let's let them decide.

00:04:26.517 --> 00:04:29.269
Bette? I know you love me.

00:04:30.812 --> 00:04:32.731
Tell them you want to stay

00:04:32.814 --> 00:04:35.275
and live forever in luxury
with me.

00:04:35.359 --> 00:04:37.361
There's something wrong
with Dandy and you know it.

00:04:44.117 --> 00:04:44.952
I'm sorry.

00:04:47.871 --> 00:04:49.206
But I choose my sister.

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:50.874
Always.

00:04:53.377 --> 00:04:54.419
We have to go.

00:04:55.671 --> 00:04:57.631
That's the only trick
you ever pulled.

00:04:58.298 --> 00:04:59.132
All our lives,

00:04:59.216 --> 00:05:01.677
you wanted everyone to think
you were the cleverer one,

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:02.678
the big brain, but...

00:05:03.804 --> 00:05:05.514
it's only
ever been about me.

00:05:05.597 --> 00:05:07.432
About trying to be me.

00:05:08.976 --> 00:05:10.310
You always thought
too small.

00:05:11.061 --> 00:05:12.938
Not like you, right?

00:05:13.772 --> 00:05:14.731
Lucifer the rebel.

00:05:15.357 --> 00:05:17.943
Deciding you can do
a better job than Dad.

00:05:20.904 --> 00:05:23.323
You know, I wonder

00:05:24.283 --> 00:05:27.202
how you got that idea
in your head

00:05:27.286 --> 00:05:28.203
in the first place.

00:05:29.705 --> 00:05:31.081
Oh, right.

00:05:31.164 --> 00:05:32.624
That's your play, is it?

00:05:32.708 --> 00:05:34.543
Taking credit
for my failed rebellion.

00:05:34.626 --> 00:05:36.503
Oh, by all means,
it's yours.

00:05:36.587 --> 00:05:38.338
Now, you see,
that is the best part.

00:05:39.214 --> 00:05:41.341
All I did
was plant the idea.

00:05:42.134 --> 00:05:43.969
You're the one
who chose to do it.

00:05:44.052 --> 00:05:48.348
You still get to keep
all the blame yourself.

00:05:52.102 --> 00:05:54.479
Your lies are so tedious,
Michael.

00:05:54.563 --> 00:05:56.815
Not as tedious
as your denial.

00:05:59.067 --> 00:06:00.861
Because I'm not lying now,
brother,

00:06:00.944 --> 00:06:03.906
and I think deep down
you are realising that.

00:06:05.449 --> 00:06:09.661
And once you realise that,
you're gonna wonder...

00:06:11.079 --> 00:06:12.873
maybe it wasn't
just the rebellion

00:06:12.956 --> 00:06:14.374
that was my suggestion.

00:06:15.375 --> 00:06:16.376
What else?

00:06:17.628 --> 00:06:18.462
What about

00:06:19.087 --> 00:06:21.381
your little sexcapade
in the garden or...

00:06:22.090 --> 00:06:25.385
oh… your vacation
here to Earth?

00:06:27.054 --> 00:06:28.347
That's impossible.

00:06:29.598 --> 00:06:31.016
It was quite easy, actually.

00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:33.310
All it took
was a little whisper here,

00:06:33.393 --> 00:06:35.354
a carefully orchestrated
coincidence there,

00:06:35.437 --> 00:06:37.981
and your pathological
self-absorption, of course,

00:06:38.065 --> 00:06:39.107
voilà!

00:06:39.650 --> 00:06:41.401
All your idea.

00:06:44.029 --> 00:06:45.656
This is nuts.

00:06:45.739 --> 00:06:46.657
We're in a void

00:06:46.740 --> 00:06:48.575
in the body
of a White lady--

00:06:48.659 --> 00:06:49.993
-Not a lady.
-Not a lady, darling.

00:06:50.077 --> 00:06:51.078
Well, we are White.

00:06:51.161 --> 00:06:52.913
Let's all say
White people things!

00:06:52.996 --> 00:06:55.457
Billy Joel.
I found it on Etsy.

00:06:55.541 --> 00:06:56.959
There was nowhere to park.

00:06:57.042 --> 00:06:58.418
Did you refill the Britta?

00:06:58.502 --> 00:07:00.420
I find this void
quite calming, actually.

00:07:00.504 --> 00:07:03.632
It's like,
this time the Xanax took me.

00:07:03.715 --> 00:07:05.634
Oh, I have the worst
stomach ache.

00:07:05.717 --> 00:07:07.427
Dude, relax!

00:07:08.053 --> 00:07:09.805
Here, let me see
if I can figure this out.

00:07:13.058 --> 00:07:15.394
Wow, Eleanor
how'd you do that?

00:07:15.477 --> 00:07:17.062
I don't know.
We're Janets now,

00:07:17.145 --> 00:07:19.189
so I thought we'd have
some bitching Janet powers.

00:07:19.273 --> 00:07:21.525
What just happened?
What did you do?

00:07:21.608 --> 00:07:23.735
Sorry, I'm just trying
to help Chidi calm down--

00:07:23.819 --> 00:07:25.279
the structural integrity
of this void

00:07:25.362 --> 00:07:26.405
is already at risk.

00:07:26.488 --> 00:07:28.699
You can't start randomly
conjuring up objects

00:07:28.782 --> 00:07:30.701
or it might shatter
the void.

00:07:30.784 --> 00:07:31.618
Yes, it might.

00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:33.495
It might
make everything blow up

00:07:33.579 --> 00:07:35.414
and we'll all
disappear forever.

00:07:36.248 --> 00:07:37.749
So, stop it!

00:07:38.792 --> 00:07:39.877
There you are!

00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:41.795
We were so worried
about you guys.

00:07:44.089 --> 00:07:45.007
Explain.

00:07:46.550 --> 00:07:48.010
Well,
Mother Superior called.

00:07:48.093 --> 00:07:50.262
Your disciplinary meeting
got pushed up,

00:07:50.345 --> 00:07:52.806
so? I had to be you.

00:07:52.890 --> 00:07:55.559
But never mind me.
Are you guys okay?

00:07:55.642 --> 00:07:58.270
More or less.
There was a bit of a hitch.

00:07:58.353 --> 00:08:00.731
Peter had to stay behind
to create a diversion.

00:08:00.814 --> 00:08:03.108
Fiona, you can't feel bad
about this.

00:08:03.192 --> 00:08:05.235
Yeah,
it really isn't your fault.

00:08:05.319 --> 00:08:07.112
Then who's fault is it?

00:08:10.699 --> 00:08:13.285
We're back! Merry Christ...

00:08:15.204 --> 00:08:16.038
What the--

00:08:16.914 --> 00:08:17.748
Who the--

00:08:18.916 --> 00:08:20.250
What's going on?

00:08:20.334 --> 00:08:21.752
I can explain everything.

00:08:21.835 --> 00:08:23.086
Which one are you?

00:08:23.170 --> 00:08:24.338
It's okay, Kev.

00:08:24.421 --> 00:08:25.923
That's Margaret, not Fiona.

00:08:26.006 --> 00:08:27.633
-Stacy?
-Yeah.

00:08:27.716 --> 00:08:29.343
And that's Margaret?

00:08:29.426 --> 00:08:31.345
-You sure?
-Let me prove it to you.

00:08:32.137 --> 00:08:33.514
No, no, no.

00:08:46.527 --> 00:08:49.530
Okay. It's you. Phew.

00:08:50.072 --> 00:08:50.989
That was really strange.

